  "text": "Làm đềtrực tuyến tại: https://ielts-fighter.com/online-test.html\nWebsite tựhọc IELTS: https://ielts-fighter.com\nFINN:\nWhen the government imposed restrictions on the use of paper.\nMAYA:\nYeah, but that was only in the UK. In the USA, programmes, or rather playbills,\ncontinued to be published in the same format.\nFINN:\nWhile here in the UK, programmes became merely a single sheet of paper\nfolded to create four MAYA:\nWhat I don’t really get is that after the war they didn’t go back to being more\nthan one sheet or change in any way for over 25 years. I know there were\npaper shortages after the war, but only for five or ten years.\nFINN:\nStrange.\nBefore you hear the rest of the discussion, you have some time to look at\nquestions 27 to 30. Now listen and answer questions 27 to 30.\nMAYA:\nI got some pictures of programmes we could include on the slides for our\npresentation.\nFINN:\nI found a couple too Maya. Let go through and see what we think.\nMAYA:\nUm oh this is an old one for a play called Ruey Blass.\nFINN:\nNever heard of that. But the programme looks very decorative.\n",
